<title>SOUTH AFRICA: EL Bateman yr share plunges, div steady.</title>
<headline>EL Bateman yr share plunges, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headlines (cts)  15.8	  vs    88.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 38.0	  vs    same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    6.73	 vs    22.69</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   13.48	 vs    35.91</p>
<p>    Tax			  8.96	 vs     6.56</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   15.55	 vs     7.54</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,697.07	 vs 1,469.22</p>
<p>    Exceptional items    (17.39)	vs    (2.55)</p>
<p>Div payable: October 25</p>
<p>On register: October 11</p>
<p>Full name: Edward L Bateman Ltd (engineering)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that losses were due to stock and debtor provisions and restructuring costs in subsidiary Bateman Industrial Corp.</p>
<p>The increase in interest paid was attributable to funding those losses as well as funding growth in profitable businesses in that company.</p>
<p>Budgets for the current year were encouraging and both listed subsidiaries were expected to improve profitability. On this basis, the company expected to see substantially improved earnings in financial 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
